---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<Base
  locale="en"
  title={`Privacy — ${site.name}`}
  description="No cookies, no trackers: the publisher collects no browsing data."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>

  <p class="meta">
    This English version is provided for convenience. In case of any discrepancy,{' '}
    <a href="/confidentialite/">the French version</a> prevails.
  </p>

  <p>
    The short version: this site is fully static. It sets <strong>no cookies</strong>, embeds{' '}
    <strong>no tracker and no analytics</strong>, and has no accounts, no forms and no third-party
    content. That is also why there is no consent banner: there is nothing to consent to. The data
    controller is the publisher of this site (see the legal notice).
  </p>

  <h2>Host technical logs</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served by Cloudflare, Inc. (USA). When you visit, Cloudflare processes technical
    data (IP address, user-agent, request metadata, security logs) to deliver the pages and keep the
    service secure (anti-DDoS, firewall) and fast. Legal basis: the publisher's legitimate interest
    in providing a safe website (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). Cloudflare acts as a processor and retains
    these logs for a limited period, as described in its privacy policy; the publisher has no access
    to raw logs.
  </p>
  <p>
    Transfers outside the European Union: Cloudflare, Inc. states that it adheres to the EU-U.S.
    Data Privacy Framework (adequacy decision (EU) 2023/1795 of 10 July 2023) and additionally
    relies on the European Commission's standard contractual clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>Demo local storage</h2>
  <p>
    Some project demos save game progress or preferences in your browser's local storage — the{' '}
    <code>localStorage</code>. That data stays on your device: nothing is sent anywhere, not to this
    site nor to third parties. This strictly functional storage is exempt from consent under Article
    82 of the French Data Protection Act. To clear it: the demo's reset button, or your browser
    settings ("clear site data").
  </p>

  <h2>Emails</h2>
  <p>
    If you write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, I receive your address and
    your message. I only use them to reply, I pass them to no one, and I keep them no longer than
    our exchange requires. Legal basis: the legitimate interest in answering the messages I am sent
    (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the rights of access, rectification, erasure, objection and restriction provided by the
    GDPR. To exercise them: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. You may also lodge a
    complaint with the French supervisory authority, the CNIL, at{' '}
    <a href="https://www.cnil.fr" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      cnil.fr
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <p class="meta">Last updated: 20 November 2026.</p>
</Base>
